{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>He skillfully crossed his hands.</b> That is: through the deed of Joseph's hands — for he placed Manasseh at his left, which is Israel's right — Jacob skillfully crossed his hands, for Manasseh was the firstborn, and despite this he placed his right hand upon Ephraim's head. And this is likened to HaShem our Elohim — [His] mercies and pardons, though we have rebelled against Him."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:17.572172998Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}